{"title":"creative systems zine: deconstructing the productivity machine","link":"https://keningzhu.com/journal/creative-systems-zine","date":1741596360000,"content":" \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5006c7d3-746b-42bc-bcd5-d5a9f4c58480/back.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"2752\" height=\"2064\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5006c7d3-746b-42bc-bcd5-d5a9f4c58480/back.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5006c7d3-746b-42bc-bcd5-d5a9f4c58480/back.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5006c7d3-746b-42bc-bcd5-d5a9f4c58480/back.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5006c7d3-746b-42bc-bcd5-d5a9f4c58480/back.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5006c7d3-746b-42bc-bcd5-d5a9f4c58480/back.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5006c7d3-746b-42bc-bcd5-d5a9f4c58480/back.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5006c7d3-746b-42bc-bcd5-d5a9f4c58480/back.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <p><em>a brief, poetic critique on productivity systems that pressurize the creative spirit — why they don’t work, and reimagining new possibilities... </em><br /><br />this zine is part of a series on building adaptive systems to support and sustain the wilderness of the creative self, inspired by my new course: <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/creative-systems\">creative systems</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/s/creative-systems-zine_deconstructing-the-machine.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">\n    download this zine\n  </a>\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <h1>how this zine was born </h1><p>on monday night I sat down to plan the syllabus for my new course, creative systems, and instead, something inside pulled me to outline a zine instead. </p><p>so, I spend the next few days making this zine — which is, basically, thinking-out-loud about <em>what a system is</em>, <em>why build a system</em>, and <em>what productivity systems I’ve deliberately left behind</em> — in search for something wilder, softer, more supportive and regenerative. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/68bcc05a-4646-4f8a-a3f6-a3c2ee7f2f10/80EF72D3-FFD1-403E-AA9D-9397386EABA4_1_105_c.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/68bcc05a-4646-4f8a-a3f6-a3c2ee7f2f10/80EF72D3-FFD1-403E-AA9D-9397386EABA4_1_105_c.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/68bcc05a-4646-4f8a-a3f6-a3c2ee7f2f10/80EF72D3-FFD1-403E-AA9D-9397386EABA4_1_105_c.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/68bcc05a-4646-4f8a-a3f6-a3c2ee7f2f10/80EF72D3-FFD1-403E-AA9D-9397386EABA4_1_105_c.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/68bcc05a-4646-4f8a-a3f6-a3c2ee7f2f10/80EF72D3-FFD1-403E-AA9D-9397386EABA4_1_105_c.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/68bcc05a-4646-4f8a-a3f6-a3c2ee7f2f10/80EF72D3-FFD1-403E-AA9D-9397386EABA4_1_105_c.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/68bcc05a-4646-4f8a-a3f6-a3c2ee7f2f10/80EF72D3-FFD1-403E-AA9D-9397386EABA4_1_105_c.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/68bcc05a-4646-4f8a-a3f6-a3c2ee7f2f10/80EF72D3-FFD1-403E-AA9D-9397386EABA4_1_105_c.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n          \n          <figcaption>\n            <p>what i sketched, in 30 minutes, on monday night — the end result looked nothing like this. </p>\n          </figcaption>\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  <p>then, the syllabus of my course emerged in 4 hefty sections — deliberately condensed to mirror the simple equation that describes a system: </p><p><strong>input + process = output (+ emergence)</strong> <br /><br />I wrote the introduction in one breath — it just unspooled from me, like a thread waiting to be pulled. </p><p>I created the rest of the zine in a two day dive, from wednesday to thursday night. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr /> \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/07cc6130-31db-4ae6-a2a6-965ceca6ae2f/2-table_of_contents.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"2752\" height=\"2064\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/07cc6130-31db-4ae6-a2a6-965ceca6ae2f/2-table_of_contents.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/07cc6130-31db-4ae6-a2a6-965ceca6ae2f/2-table_of_contents.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/07cc6130-31db-4ae6-a2a6-965ceca6ae2f/2-table_of_contents.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/07cc6130-31db-4ae6-a2a6-965ceca6ae2f/2-table_of_contents.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/07cc6130-31db-4ae6-a2a6-965ceca6ae2f/2-table_of_contents.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/07cc6130-31db-4ae6-a2a6-965ceca6ae2f/2-table_of_contents.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/07cc6130-31db-4ae6-a2a6-965ceca6ae2f/2-table_of_contents.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n <hr />\n\n\n  <h1>the introduction text of my zine + course</h1><p><em>what are systems, beyond structures of imprisonment, extraction, and control? </em></p><p><em>why build systems for the wilderness of the creative spirit, and how do we do it without diminishing or killing its essence? </em></p><p><em>it starts with getting the machinery of “productivity” out of our heads — deprogramming as liberation. then, slowly, cultivating a new relationship with our inner and life resources — time, attention, energy, inspiration — not as limited reserves to mine, or hoard, or control — but as fluid entities, like the weather, or the ebb and flow of the tidal waves, or the moon. </em></p><p><em>therefore, the systems we build for human/cosmic/natural bodies must be born from deep observation. inquiry. listening. surrender. response. we ask it what it needs to feel held and safe. to rest, and dream. reimagine, and expand. </em></p><p><em>we reinvent our systems, like writing our own languages. trusting them to speak for us — to make new worlds of care, possibility, and regeneration. </em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr /> \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f1bf62f0-962d-4bbf-aabd-7c6488e3b26b/3-what_is_a_system.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"2752\" height=\"2064\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f1bf62f0-962d-4bbf-aabd-7c6488e3b26b/3-what_is_a_system.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f1bf62f0-962d-4bbf-aabd-7c6488e3b26b/3-what_is_a_system.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f1bf62f0-962d-4bbf-aabd-7c6488e3b26b/3-what_is_a_system.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f1bf62f0-962d-4bbf-aabd-7c6488e3b26b/3-what_is_a_system.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f1bf62f0-962d-4bbf-aabd-7c6488e3b26b/3-what_is_a_system.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f1bf62f0-962d-4bbf-aabd-7c6488e3b26b/3-what_is_a_system.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f1bf62f0-962d-4bbf-aabd-7c6488e3b26b/3-what_is_a_system.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n <hr />\n\n\n  <h1>deconstructing the (productivity) machine </h1><p>after writing that introduction, I felt like I found the skeletal structure and bone marrow / guiding spirit for the course. </p><p>then, I actually intended to write a short chapter on each of the four sections — to give a bird’s eye view of what I’ll be diving into during the 4 weeks. but once I started writing part 1 — deconstructing the machine — I found that I had so much to say about traditional productivity systems that I couldn’t stop writing. I realized how important the work of reframing and deprogramming really is, and how embedded it is into the psyche — like a virus that never dies.</p><p>I first wrote about this programming — being an “<a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/self-care-for-accomplishment-junkies\" target=\"_blank\">accomplishment junkie</a>” — in 2019, back when I was very much still entrenched the productivity/hustle mindset. in 2023, I identifed the head static of <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/head-static-am-i-doing-enough\" target=\"_blank\">“am I doing enough?”</a> — as its own frequency that buzzes in the background. </p><p>years later, the buzzing static is very much reduced. but, I still catch it. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr /> \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5b6c3358-7f70-4292-af17-d0c3b1554cc0/blank.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"2752\" height=\"2064\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5b6c3358-7f70-4292-af17-d0c3b1554cc0/blank.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5b6c3358-7f70-4292-af17-d0c3b1554cc0/blank.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5b6c3358-7f70-4292-af17-d0c3b1554cc0/blank.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5b6c3358-7f70-4292-af17-d0c3b1554cc0/blank.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5b6c3358-7f70-4292-af17-d0c3b1554cc0/blank.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5b6c3358-7f70-4292-af17-d0c3b1554cc0/blank.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5b6c3358-7f70-4292-af17-d0c3b1554cc0/blank.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n <hr />\n\n\n  <h1>future zines </h1><p>this was my first zine since this <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/sleep-zine\" target=\"_blank\">sleep zine</a> I made in 2022, which definitely felt different to create. I’m curious to continue exploring the zine form — is it something between a mini-book, and a visual exploration? </p><p>I’m not sure if I’ll be creating zines for the other 3 chapter sections — for now, I’ve decided to dedicate my energy to making the course. by the time I’ve done that, I will probably get distracted/excited about something entirely new. </p><p>but, definitely, definitely more zines coming soon. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr /> \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/cdd8fe99-56bd-4526-aded-6839dcd774f7/back+1.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"2752\" height=\"2064\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/cdd8fe99-56bd-4526-aded-6839dcd774f7/back+1.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/cdd8fe99-56bd-4526-aded-6839dcd774f7/back+1.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/cdd8fe99-56bd-4526-aded-6839dcd774f7/back+1.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/cdd8fe99-56bd-4526-aded-6839dcd774f7/back+1.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/cdd8fe99-56bd-4526-aded-6839dcd774f7/back+1.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/cdd8fe99-56bd-4526-aded-6839dcd774f7/back+1.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/cdd8fe99-56bd-4526-aded-6839dcd774f7/back+1.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/s/creative-systems-zine_deconstructing-the-machine.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">\n    download the zine\n  </a>\n\n\n\n\n  <p><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/creative-systems\">explore creative systems course</a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr /> ","author":"Kening Zhu","siteTitle":"kening zhu","siteHash":"ef8a94b9fc20c32a4ee7d94ee971337d278e8b2fafe747123e4eb5cea026e84e","entryHash":"9e39a2485b789fa14ca4f31176f065b6c38cf18193c582529b045c87894f58a3","category":"Sites"}